 "type": "concept", "title": "Prophecy"}, {"id": "5e595cfc-4e58-4514-bfb2-e16b4f53d25e", "type": "concept", "title": "Spiritual gifts"}, {"id": "862a3a63-3ef3-434a-9b02-abda4facdb58", "type": "concept", "title": "Global networks"}, {"id": "59fc3510-ea06-4b2d-94a9-f7b4fe04bb42", "type": "concept", "title": "Media ministries"}], "description": "The goal is to understand Pentecostal influence beyond Pentecostal denominations."}]}, {"id": "247e1a3d-3683-4ceb-af59-fc67237ec7f3", "type": "topic", "title": "Christianity and Politics", "description": "Christian communities have supported, resisted, justified, and transformed political orders. This unit studies public religion, nationalism, democracy, empire, violence, liberation, and civil rights.", "children": [{"id": "740f53dd-2642-4d36-b1ca-8570b7639586", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Church, state, and nation", "children": [{"id": "995e4c7c-384c-441c-a4f2-a4321bcd649e", "type": "concept", "title": "Established churches"}, {"id": "7b359d9f-570a-4906-b4f1-b19735d336fd", "type": "concept", "title": "Religious liberty"}, {"id": "fdc890b7-11e6-4597-a3a9-2ad546082685", "type": "concept", "title": "Christian nationalism"}, {"id": "38f733ef-c5c7-4d1c-884a-fe40767a78d9", "type": "concept", "title": "Theocracy"}, {"id": "693c172c-b6a6-4e2a-a8da-c4c4c97e364d", "type": "concept", "title": "Secularism"}, {"id": "dd45ca5b-7f44-40be-b9c1-286b69153600", "type": "concept", "title": "Concordats"}, {"id": "f62fc439-98f2-4396-8672-b88fb170fa74", "type": "concept", "title": "Civil religion"}, {"id": "b806fb93-445d-4907-bf2d-b70cfd406bb9", "type": "concept", "title": "Public theology"}], "description": "Students learn how Christian institutions relate to political authority in different settings."}, {"id": "273a3b0b-e592-4cd7-8cde-7a77014ee525", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Christianity, empire, and violence", "children": [{"id": "9546a0ec-47d4-4584-93ae-61d5036fad80", "type": "concept", "title": "Just war"}, {"id": "907a2eb9-59c4-42a8-b618-40cda130f464", "type": "concept", "title": "Pacifism"}, {"id": "2044e294-d2c6-4c25-8e8a-34c41534bea3", "type": "concept", "title": "Crusading memory"}, {"id": "ccd1469d-ba13-4ca2-84d9-778ca9007b90", "type": "concept", "title": "Colonial rule"}, {"id": "fecb64e8-b96f-4a90-8a8d-e0ccc4ecd412", "type": "concept", "title": "World wars"}, {"id": "71823ba4-e388-4891-8af3-c54cf9a48bb3", "type": "concept", "title": "Chaplaincy"}, {"id": "aa95f979-de72-499f-93ba-08d08832d337", "type": "concept", "title": "Genocide"}, {"id": "84fb8784-ddd6-4bfa-a8ff-ebe3870becc3", "type": "concept", "title": "Reconciliation"}], "description": "Students examine Christian participation in and resistance to imperial and military power."}, {"id": "1b714385-4635-4199-86e6-2b8d4f0fd32e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Liberation and civil rights", "children": [{"id": "5b80173f-33e8-4d09-bebc-54ced364488b", "type": "concept", "title": "Black church"}, {"id": "7b85cc54-6c93-4f35-8eda-1ed4d9529e02", "type": "concept", "title": "Civil rights movement"}, {"id": "e77265dc-8b43-405b-bffd-f58edebd19c8", "type": "concept", "title": "Martin Luther King Jr."}, {"id": "1c07882d-1034-4dbb-9a03-8ecebed77af1", "type": "concept", "title": "Liberation theology"}, {"id": "59de2df7-857f-42d7-b8a0-b721a49fd191", "type": "concept", "title": "Base communities"}, {"id": "b189d657-6c2f-445b-9220-b1337ea54010", "type": "concept", "title": "Anti-apartheid Christianity"}, {"id": "0631f462-85ae-471b-90b7-c35ec7ef7cb5", "type": "concept", "title": "Feminist theology"}, {"id": "fcd53b0f-4f4a-4ef1-80bd-ef80e163bc40", "type": "concept", "title": "Dalit theology"}], "description": "The point is to see Christianity as a resource for social movements and as an object of critique."}]}, {"id": "f042ec2a-2d88-4673-945c-2419b52f55bd", "type": "topic", "title": "Modern Missions and Global Christianity", "description": "Christianity is now a global tradition with major centers beyond Europe and North America. Students examine demographic change, local theologies, migration, and the re-centering of Christian history.", "children": [{"id": "174072c2-6aa5-4905-943e-89eecfdeacf3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Global demographic shifts", "children": [{"id": "a27eb580-7881-4026-820f-a5b2ec74fb97", "type": "concept", "title": "Global South"}, {"id": "22ec8a39-9603-4937-9c4c-b19160a3fd9e", "type": "concept", "title": "African Christianity"}, {"id": "9428e967-c2ff-467e-ac24-6ca4b57f624d", "type": "concept", "title": "Latin American Christianity"}, {"id": "6e440668-267e-4444-a392-8810afc3a5c8", "type": "concept", "title": "Asian Christianity"}, {"id": "3f5add5f-dc22-4dda-8671-5602298eb20a", "type": "concept", "title": "Pacific Christianity"}, {"id": "dc03fbd0-061b-425e-81fe-043eb1014a9b", "type": "concept", "title": "Migration"}, {"id": "8df73448-7657-4be3-b126-6ef46df30780", "type": "concept", "title": "Diaspora churches"}, {"id": "aaa96f5b-ca17-4643-9db4-ce95c117c0e9", "type": "concept", "title": "Urban Christianity"}], "description": "Students learn how the geographic center of Christianity changed over the twentieth century."}, {"id": "720aa457-5f32-49dc-b8be-bcdd2a57d31c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Local theologies and practices", "children": [{"id": "45bc7864-56a8-43d5-8600-5ff66da1e437", "type": "concept", "title": "Inculturation"}, {"id": "edde87c3-a7c7-4f99-9d2e-fa16f46d5f76", "type": "concept", "title": "Contextual theology"}, {"id": "b630fff6-3ec1-466f-a93b-45f9ac20f04f", "type": "concept", "title": "African independent churches"}, {"id": "6bf38b03-b8b2-42a2-86f5-d785b89772e1", "type": "concept", "title": "Minjung theology"}, {"id": "3806069c-a8c2-4465-9f2b-4f1a8db29413", "type": "concept", "title": "Base communities"}, {"id": "843813c0-344d-4133-96e1-90ef623e7e11", "type": "concept", "title": "Indigenous theology"}, {"id": "439c4847-aac7-478a-b9a2-1c9a85461af4", "type": "concept", "title": "Postcolonial theology"}, {"id": "6b36da85-1a93-4de4-b04c-818b22fb61cb", "type": "concept", "title": "Vernacular Bible"}], "description": "Students examine how communities interpret Christianity through local histories, cultures, and struggles."}, {"id": "f49527eb-08a7-4909-a430-cade85f071a7", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Ecumenism and world Christianity", "children": [{"id": "20062a7e-e9af-4a1b-90ef-f79469a70f50", "type": "concept", "title": "World Council of Churches"}, {"id": "b4cd6cb8-8ea0-44be-a361-11e7e6facda5", "type": "concept", "title": "Edinburgh 1910"}, {"id": "f937748b-310d-4d54-b5e0-30fea6accec3", "type": "concept", "title": "Lausanne movement"}, {"id": "b7fe3a41-dd25-46cd-a544-5564e09ab35c", "type": "concept", "title": "Ecumenical dialogue"}, {"id": "29d97c9d-4d87-45a4-ae10-bd555a58f39a", "type": "concept", "title": "Interfaith relations"}, {"id": "627948ee-76fb-476c-b32c-45f43df3a9d0", "type": "concept", "title": "Global Catholicism"}, {"id": "e4267516-f397-4ebb-8f17-04e74a84ab93", "type": "concept", "title": "Orthodox diaspora"}, {"id": "e4d263de-1c31-41ad-ad9b-33cdb86d075e", "type": "concept", "title": "World Christianity"}], "description": "The goal is to understand Christianity as a connected but internally diverse global field."}]}, {"id": "d692747f-ad2d-4913-ac63-60e9f6db1238", "type": "topic", "title": "Christianity, Society, Gender, Race, and Everyday Life", "description": "Christian history is not only theology and institutions; it is also bodies, households, labor, ritual, music, art, race, gender, sexuality, class, and everyday practice. This unit brings social history into the center.", "children": [{"id": "650a7fad-e0f2-450d-a745-389a63c0d00f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Gender and authority", "children": [{"id": "e8c82ba2-ea7a-42b1-bf0e-3356ad232261", "type": "concept", "title": "Women leaders"}, {"id": "17373e58-951e-4743-aca5-25fe2149eeea", "type": "concept", "title": "Female monasticism"}, {"id": "9bc11cea-2973-40f4-9c23-1ab5488660a0", "type": "concept", "title": "Mary devotion"}, {"id": "963ac2af-5b1c-47a6-af96-5a4a22785aec", "type": "concept", "title": "Ordination debates"}, {"id": "b68b983b-0c6e-4c5d-9d09-4497b22f2acd", "type": "concept", "title": "Complementarianism"}, {"id": "2db46c61-16b6-4fbe-ac37-8e059e4c05be", "type": "concept", "title": "Egalitarianism"}, {"id": "df13d073-5e3d-48b1-ac8b-9968e9509766", "type": "concept", "title": "Purity culture"}, {"id": "cc8dbf87-3098-46bb-bf72-adbeaae10689", "type": "concept", "title": "Feminist theology"}], "description": "Students examine how Christian communities have constructed, contested, and changed gender roles."}, {"id": "197eebd6-d56a-4f1c-9a1d-edc899ab6630", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Race, slavery, and colonial legacies", "children": [{"id": "c0c5b4f0-e77b-4b77-9b08-3108d996134a", "type": "concept", "title": "Atlantic slavery"}, {"id": "7ae37c33-4baa-4d9c-97f2-e665c1d41e8f", "type": "concept", "title": "Abolitionism"}, {"id": "0d4cc810-461c-467e-b9bc-9ee9266bbe2f", "type": "concept", "title": "Slave religion"}, {"id": "2ef85707-0622-4e67-9da2-e0c642f91a53", "type": "concept", "title": "Segregated churches"}, {"id": "9784d81a-196d-460f-82de-ba8c2548d525", "type": "concept", "title": "Mission schools"}, {"id": "b7bcf88d-ad48-4d1c-9aaf-48a72c9f90c4", "type": "concept", "title": "Indigenous boarding schools"}, {"id": "92090357-3292-47e3-8012-a1733055f8ae", "type": "concept", "title": "Anti-racism"}, {"id": "cb9ee89b-3ef3-4e32-abbb-8bf782b6ee53", "type": "concept", "title": "Reparations debates"}], "description": "Students learn how Christianity has been used to justify domination and to inspire resistance."}, {"id": "2b27964f-cc46-41c3-9866-df5ce2709546", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Everyday Christian practice", "children": [{"id": "4fb975fd-199f-4850-abb9-dc94b0b0c7b2", "type": "concept", "title": "Prayer"}, {"id": "cba7c9ad-7f9d-4a66-be41-51a4809a633a", "type": "concept", "title": "Hymns"}, {"id": "c97a1074-a052-4e6b-aed4-ab1321c913db", "type": "concept", "title": "Icons"}, {"id": "417aedc7-2e4a-451b-b62d-9c0ccc6017e7", "type": "concept", "title": "Pilgrimage"}, {"id": "15fbb838-85ba-42c0-aa04-1e29ded53893", "type": "concept", "title": "Fasting"}, {"id": "1e3fa906-4234-440f-90f4-44af0594d210", "type": "concept", "title": "Feasts"}, {"id": "5e1052fc-0da6-47e4-b49f-b6a26b8e698c", "type": "concept", "title": "Family religion"}, {"id": "db968e8a-da64-4e87-8727-8734170e5f7b", "type": "concept", "title": "Healing"}, {"id": "bffa84a7-554c-4ea4-a9ae-1cb38a158e3e", "type": "concept", "title": "Material religion"}], "description": "The point is to study lived religion beyond official doctrine."}]}, {"id": "224491fb-6cb9-4da7-bf24-ff4d4f822a40", "type": "topic", "title": "Contemporary Theological Debates and the Future of Christianity", "description": "The final unit asks students to connect long historical trajectories to present debates without collapsing history into present concerns. Students learn how contemporary Christianity debates authority, identity, knowledge, ethics, and survival.", "children": [{"id": "f2692ff5-abb5-447e-ae1b-256a475ac0b8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Authority and interpretation", "children": [{"id": "d2631057-6c9d-44c7-894b-64f8c0b2ed3c", "type": "concept", "title": "Biblical authority"}, {"id": "3f2511b0-c0f1-4a60-b49f-1e8f0b652027", "type": "concept", "title": "Tradition"}, {"id": "95bf7ebc-914e-4208-bff5-99a704fd3d56", "type": "concept", "title": "Magisterium"}, {"id": "5f290fc1-3fba-4ba0-ba72-cd8704cc75a7", "type": "concept", "title": "Inerrancy"}, {"id": "1ad4e55e-d0ac-40c6-9b23-edc371c06838", "type": "concept", "title": "Hermeneutics"}, {"id": "42014e52-7cc1-4fb0-926e-7119ae7f63f7", "type": "concept", "title": "Historical criticism"}, {"id": "5a0ec549-ea7f-40fe-b989-98a677624c4f", "type": "concept", "title": "Reception history"}, {"id": "315cb660-85be-4f25-ade2-b9cb3da73e64", "type": "concept", "title": "Public theology"}], "description": "Students examine how Christians debate scripture, tradition, reason, experience, and institutional authority."}, {"id": "2bcaa503-8777-401b-a110-208f8c49d67a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Ethical and social debates", "children": [{"id": "78479b59-5fa4-4fc5-8587-65cbc865232d", "type": "concept", "title": "Gender and sexuality"}, {"id": "5f2c753a-529e-4000-a12a-02523dc45213", "type": "concept", "title": "Abortion"}, {"id": "7b00a0c9-3ced-409d-a746-09ec5ba7759c", "type": "concept", "title": "Climate change"}, {"id": "36dacaab-5c3c-44fe-ae89-247595b59694", "type": "concept", "title": "Economic justice"}, {"id": "0f5b6109-f219-468b-bc00-adf31418d3b3", "type": "concept", "title": "War and peace"}, {"id": "4f1f246f-d267-4aed-b466-cd1d0426552f", "type": "concept", "title": "Migration"}, {"id": "628c5358-0ccc-444e-ae6a-68aab3a6ffa9", "type": "concept", "title": "Racial justice"}, {"id": "81606c91-04d7-4442-9962-786d3c689fb3", "type": "concept", "title": "Medical ethics"}], "description": "Students place contemporary disputes in historical perspective."}, {"id": "7f6f5767-0a7c-406d-8958-deaef66aedb1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Future directions", "children": [{"id": "2e4ae8ba-5abf-4cf2-a29f-190cb98800d3", "type": "concept", "title": "Secularization"}, {"id": "c2ee43b0-4e6c-4024-9bcc-115bfdd90d44", "type": "concept", "title": "Religious switching"}, {"id": "0ae1d1e4-7898-4ae8-860c-855491e2ac85", "type": "concept", "title": "Nones"}, {"id": "98d81713-a13c-497c-9a3e-9f923c5d758b", "type": "concept", "title": "Digital religion"}, {"id": "b5ee786d-b172-4cc4-b9ab-23cb6d980a48", "type": "concept", "title": "Artificial intelligence"}, {"id": "00396563-434f-46a8-b44b-e446c153faa8", "type": "concept", "title": "Interfaith engagement"}, {"id": "945f5638-af7e-4ded-a5d3-ad4a3afa6ed6", "type": "concept", "title": "Persecution"}, {"id": "09764415-b07b-4791-ad94-03915972f8b0", "type": "concept", "title": "Ecological crisis"}, {"id": "41552950-1a18-4545-902f-cfb4d365916c", "type": "concept", "title": "Global demographics"}], "description": "The goal is to identify major pressures shaping Christianity's future."}]