aints' lives"}], "description": "The goal is to understand experiential, affective, and embodied forms of Christian practice."}]}, {"id": "a4977a75-46ba-4d6b-a8eb-fbce9f41478e", "type": "topic", "title": "Eastern Orthodoxy and Byzantine Christianity", "description": "Eastern Christianity developed distinctive theological, liturgical, political, and artistic traditions. This unit centers Byzantine, Syriac, Coptic, Armenian, and Slavic Christian worlds rather than treating them as side stories.", "children": [{"id": "3e7f3dcd-3d86-4a08-a2ec-e7210712c99f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Byzantine church and empire", "children": [{"id": "a5d41244-0fa9-493c-8960-5daccdadc310", "type": "concept", "title": "Constantinople"}, {"id": "2ece55ce-319d-48ec-a9ec-7d8ccfa9457a", "type": "concept", "title": "Hagia Sophia"}, {"id": "09f3f31b-a2fb-4f2d-8f0b-89e20cbaecf2", "type": "concept", "title": "Patriarch"}, {"id": "a4c3ea7f-cb93-42f9-ab45-282e153a3ee6", "type": "concept", "title": "Caesaropapism debates"}, {"id": "495492fc-e0b7-4deb-9fef-7803b70b9e60", "type": "concept", "title": "Iconoclasm"}, {"id": "72a2e2e8-dd2c-4fb8-9e94-303c6c455568", "type": "concept", "title": "Iconodules"}, {"id": "4032c3ef-a597-4338-bb3e-ed92ac96edc3", "type": "concept", "title": "Icons"}, {"id": "82713e3f-81e0-4593-ba9c-018500ed0150", "type": "concept", "title": "Liturgy"}], "description": "Students learn how Christianity functioned in the Eastern Roman Empire."}, {"id": "93dbde4e-7f33-48ee-9ceb-a6058a0e1eb9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Eastern theology and spirituality", "children": [{"id": "a6a5dfb0-241f-4357-b592-a7eb1d74381c", "type": "concept", "title": "Theosis"}, {"id": "1f66547f-a8c8-4a91-a2e4-8d4f24b67e29", "type": "concept", "title": "Apophatic theology"}, {"id": "f2366941-8bb4-4eaf-a133-de7e14004cec", "type": "concept", "title": "Desert spirituality"}, {"id": "2cec3dc1-2439-43a2-8399-e7f51247650c", "type": "concept", "title": "Hesychasm"}, {"id": "61b3ced6-d383-42de-8afc-3bda8d75a6a9", "