": "Vernacular Bible"}], "description": "Students examine how communities interpret Christianity through local histories, cultures, and struggles."}, {"id": "f49527eb-08a7-4909-a430-cade85f071a7", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Ecumenism and world Christianity", "children": [{"id": "20062a7e-e9af-4a1b-90ef-f79469a70f50", "type": "concept", "title": "World Council of Churches"}, {"id": "b4cd6cb8-8ea0-44be-a361-11e7e6facda5", "type": "concept", "title": "Edinburgh 1910"}, {"id": "f937748b-310d-4d54-b5e0-30fea6accec3", "type": "concept", "title": "Lausanne movement"}, {"id": "b7fe3a41-dd25-46cd-a544-5564e09ab35c", "type": "concept", "title": "Ecumenical dialogue"}, {"id": "29d97c9d-4d87-45a4-ae10-bd555a58f39a", "type": "concept", "title": "Interfaith relations"}, {"id": "627948ee-76fb-476c-b32c-45f43df3a9d0", "type": "concept", "title": "Global Catholicism"}, {"id": "e4267516-f397-4ebb-8f17-04e74a84ab93", "type": "concept", "title": "Orthodox diaspora"}, {"id": "e4d263de-1c31-41ad-ad9b-33cdb86d075e", "type": "concept", "title": "World Christianity"}], "description": "The goal is to understand Christianity as a connected but internally diverse global field."}]}, {"id": "d692747f-ad2d-4913-ac63-60e9f6db1238", "type": "topic", "title": "Christianity, Society, Gender, Race, and Everyday Life", "description": "Christian history is not only theology and institutions; it is also bodies, households, labor, ritual, music, art, race, gender, sexuality, class, and everyday practice. This unit brings social history into the center.", "children": [{"id": "650a7fad-e0f2-450d-a745-389a63c0d00f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Gender and authority", "children": [{"id": "e8c82ba2-ea7a-42b1-bf0e-3356ad232261", "type": "concept", "title": "Women leaders"}, {"id": "17373e58-951e-4743-aca5-25fe2149eeea", "type": "concept", "title": "Female monasticism"}, {"id": "9bc11cea-2973-40f4-9c23-1ab5488660a0", "type": "concept", "title": "Mary devotion"}, {"id": "963ac2af-5b1c-47a6-af96-5a4a22785aec",